      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, the delivery handover must confirm that the vehicle’s condition matches the documentation captured at pickup and that mileage records are accurate. Performing the handover in daylight ensures that visual inspections are clear and that any discrepancies can be identified without reliance on artificial lighting.</p>

<p>The process is divided into three core activities: daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification against the logistics receipt (LR) bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off by both the driver and the receiving party.</p>

